# %% [markdown]
# ## Sec. 5: bitcoin-attack
# **Claim:** Storm builds, minimises and exports the bitcoin-attack MA to UMB in under 3 s (11475 states, 7551 after minimisation); mcsta checks the time-bounded reachability property on it in 13 s; Storm with Unif+ gives no result within 2 minutes.<br>
# **Estimated evaluation time:** 3 minutes
#
# `%time` prints the wall-clock time of a command (`Wall time`; the CPU times are those of Python only).

# %%
import os

CLAIM = "/artifact/claims/3-sec5-bitcoin-attack"
os.makedirs("/tmp/3-sec5-bitcoin-attack", exist_ok=True)
os.chdir("/tmp/3-sec5-bitcoin-attack")
!cp {CLAIM}/ba.jani {CLAIM}/ba.properties.txt .

# %% [markdown]
# Storm builds, minimises and exports the model.
# The paper's command is obsolete, as its `--janiproperty` also makes Storm check the properties (the last step below); `--prop` here only gives Storm the target states, so the model is slightly smaller than in the paper: 11375 states, 7403 after minimisation.

# %%
%time !storm --jani ba.jani -const MALICIOUS=40,CD=50 --prop "((m_len >= 50) & (m_diff > 0))" -e dd-to-sparse --bisimulation --exportbuild ba.umb

# %% [markdown]
# mcsta checks the property in 13 s with the switch-step algorithm (`Probability: 0.15435216442756577`):

# %%
# mcsta currently requires the initial state to be state 0, while Storm puts it at an arbitrary index.
# umb_reorder.py moves it to index 0 (a temporary workaround, not in the paper).
!python {CLAIM}/umb_reorder.py ba.umb ba-reordered.umb
# Input from /dev/null: mcsta's progress display crashes in a container terminal
%time !modest mcsta ba-reordered.umb ba.properties.txt --time-bounded-alg SwitchStep < /dev/null

# %% [markdown]
# Storm checks the property itself with Unif+ (the paper's command, without the export): 11475 states, 7551 after minimisation, as in the paper, and no result within 2 minutes.

# %%
# Unif+ is Storm's default for time-bounded reachability on MAs
%time !timeout 120 storm --jani ba.jani -const MALICIOUS=40,CD=50 --janiproperty -e dd-to-sparse --bisimulation
print("no result (time limit)" if _exit_code == 124 else f"exit code {_exit_code}")
